>Re hooks: does it matter whether a hook is a macro or a token
>register?

Token registers can be modified more efficently and and in an
easier manner. It is simple enough to say

\toklist={\the\toklist <extra stuff>}
\toklist={<extra stuff> \the\toklist}

The parallel actions in a macro are somewhat more complicated.

